comments.body:
The current codebase never checks the return value.  Effectively we always assume that things go fine.  So I have just changed the behaviour willy-nilly.

Note: The idea of patching the environment with every call is that we set the behaviour we want, and then afterwards, we restore the setting to whatever value the user had before calling us.  Since we're a library we cannot set other people's globals such as envvars, but we can make these adjustments for our own good as long as nobody finds out.

@ajjackson  this is basically as discussed at the last maintainer meeting.  OK with you?
